# Scanner output. Every lab writes its reports into exercises/ when you run the
# scripts, and those are regenerated on each run -- they are not source.
*/exercises/*.json
*/exercises/*.sarif
*/exercises/*.html
*/exercises/*.txt
*/exercises/*.tsv
*/exercises/*.pcap
*/exercises/prowler/
*/exercises/web-scan.*

# Generated TLS material and SBOMs
*/exercises/*.cdx.json
*/exercises/*.spdx.json

# Lab 02 builds a throwaway git repo with planted secrets. It is generated by
# scripts/init-sample-repo.sh and must never be committed (an embedded .git also
# confuses the parent repo).
02-secrets-detection/sample-repo/

# Fixtures containing real-shaped (but fake) credentials. Generated by each lab's
# scripts/plant-secrets.sh rather than committed: a correctly shaped credential in a
# committed file is a credential to GitHub's push protection, and it blocks the push.
# The generators live in 09-security/scripts/fake-secrets.sh.
01-vulnerability-scanning/apps/vulnerable-node/.env.sample
04-container-security/insecure/Dockerfile
!04-container-security/insecure/Dockerfile.tmpl

# Lab 08 generates a Wazuh certificate authority + node certs on first setup.
08-incident-response/certs/
08-incident-response/config/certs.yml.lock

# Lab 09 answer file written by the learner during exercise 6.
09-network-security/exercises/min-firewall.md

# node_modules from the sample apps (lab 01 / 03 / 04 / 10)
**/node_modules/
**/package-lock.json

# ...but these ARE source and must stay tracked.
!*/exercises/renovate.json
!*/exercises/dependabot.json
